<item><title>Namibia sets N$18 hourly minimum for security guards from January 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-sets-n-18-hourly-minimum-for-security-guards-from-0b5c2e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-sets-n-18-hourly-minimum-for-security-guards-from-0b5c2e/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The final stage of a three-year wage transition will lift the minimum from N$16 and cover more than 30 000 workers nationwide.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:11:28 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-sets-n-18-hourly-minimum-for-security-guards-from-0b5c2e/share.jpg" length="42756" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-sets-n-18-hourly-minimum-for-security-guards-from-0b5c2e/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gondwana shares begin trading on Namibia’s OTC market at N$9.60</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/gondwana-shares-begin-trading-on-namibia-s-otc-market-at-n-d9abf8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/gondwana-shares-begin-trading-on-namibia-s-otc-market-at-n-d9abf8/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The tourism group’s shares are available through four stockbrokers, but its OTC quotation does not raise new capital and trades can be infrequent.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:50:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Telecom Namibia reports equipment thefts at northern sites</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/telecom-namibia-reports-equipment-thefts-at-northern-sites-3c25ab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/telecom-namibia-reports-equipment-thefts-at-northern-sites-3c25ab/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The break-ins damaged infrastructure at sites in Oshakati, Ongwediva and Ondangwa, disrupting voice and data services, the company said.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:27:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia&apos;s EU exports rise more than 17% to N$17.6 billion</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-s-eu-exports-rise-more-than-17-to-n-17-6-billion-fcfeac/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-s-eu-exports-rise-more-than-17-to-n-17-6-billion-fcfeac/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Exports to the bloc supported an estimated 40 000 direct jobs in 2025, a study presented in Windhoek found, with the EU now taking 19.4% of the country&apos;s total exports.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:06:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia vehicle sales fall 6.2% to 1,188 in October</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-vehicle-sales-fall-6-2-to-1-188-in-october-b0f4b9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-vehicle-sales-fall-6-2-to-1-188-in-october-b0f4b9/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Toyota registrations dropped by 106 from a year earlier, ending the market’s 18-month run of annual growth despite gains across other brands.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:56:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
